            [ 'The gap between how people answer and how they actually behave', '<p>A well-documented pattern in behavioral finance: people often answer risk questionnaires more aggressively when markets are calm and rising, then panic-sell during an actual downturn — the opposite of what their stated risk tolerance would predict. If you\'ve never lived through a real 20%+ market drop with real money invested, treat your quiz answer as a starting estimate, not a guarantee of how you\'ll actually react.</p>' ],
