            [ 'Why exchange rates move day to day', '<p>Currency values shift constantly based on interest rate differences between countries, economic data releases, political events, and overall market sentiment. A currency from a country raising interest rates often strengthens, since higher rates attract foreign capital seeking a better return — this is one of the main mechanisms behind day-to-day rate movements, though far from the only one.</p>' ],
            [ 'Sending money abroad vs. converting cash', '<p>A wire transfer or international payment app and a physical currency exchange are not the same transaction and often carry very different total costs. Transfer services increasingly disclose their exact exchange rate and fee upfront, which makes it possible to directly compare the total received against this reference rate — do that comparison before committing to any single provider for a large transfer.</p>' ],
